# The build context is the repository. Almost nothing is excluded, and the exclusions are listed
# rather than assumed.
#
# `.git` IS INCLUDED, and that is the one line to read before editing this file. Version identity is
# established by comparing the executing tree against the release tag it claims to be, the release
# gate reads commit ancestry, and the content-identity primitive resolves blobs from the committed
# tree at a revision. Excluding `.git` here would not fail those checks — it would make them report
# that they could not tell, which is worse, because the pipeline would stay green.
#
# There is no `node_modules` line either. This repository has none (ADR 0001); adding a defensive
# exclusion for a directory that must never exist would quietly normalise its existence.

# The local-CI result document. Excluded so that a previous run's output is not part of the context
# that produces the next one, which is what makes a rebuild deterministic.
artifacts/local-ci/
